From: Rainist7heta <thetamkz621@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:35:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] davs2: make the endian check pass under clang

The configure script rewrites its endian probe into
`strings conftest.o | grep -q bss`, which assumes the compiler always emits a
.bss section, even an empty one. clang omits empty sections, so the check
aborts on a little-endian target.

Look for .text and .data instead; both compilers emit them.

---
 build/linux/configure | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/linux/configure b/build/linux/configure
index ac90f74..c67c6f9 100755
--- a/build/linux/configure
+++ b/build/linux/configure
@@ -926,7 +926,10 @@
     if (${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -q BIGE) && (${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -q FPendian) ; then
         define WORDS_BIGENDIAN
         CPU_ENDIAN="big-endian"
-    elif !(${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -q EGIB && ${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -q naidnePF) ; then
+    # NOTE: upstream's sed above rewrites this check to `grep -q bss`, which
+    # assumes gcc always emits a (possibly empty) .bss section. clang omits
+    # empty sections, so use tokens both compilers emit.
+    elif !(${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -qF .text && ${cross_prefix}strings -a conftest.o | grep -qF .data) ; then
         die "endian test failed"
     fi
 fi
